1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:10,700
March 1989. Mark Kilroy, a twenty-one-year-old pre-med student from the University of Texas, crossed into Matamoros for spring break. Outside a bar, he vanished.

2
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:15,650
His family searched. Authorities on both sides of the border searched. For weeks, nothing.

3
00:00:15,670 --> 00:00:25,980
Then, on April 1st, a drug trafficker named Serafín Hernández drove straight through a police checkpoint. According to later accounts, he believed rituals had made him invisible.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,410
Police followed him to a ranch outside the city: Rancho Santa Elena.

5
00:00:30,430 --> 00:00:35,340
There they found a ritual cauldron… and fifteen bodies. One of them was Mark Kilroy.

6
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:44,480
Their leader was Adolfo de Jesús Constanzo, El Padrino. He promised his followers that human sacrifice would protect them from bullets and from the police.

7
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:52,020
Weeks later, police cornered him in Mexico City. On May 6th, 1989, he ordered one of his own followers to shoot him.

8
00:00:52,040 --> 00:01:00,781
No trial. No answers. The cult that thought it was invisible was exposed by the one family that wouldn't stop looking. This is Plot Twist with A&R.

